From 94871573750ac330445a136f26f563fa9b769508 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:54:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Build warnings-clean with Linux clang and GCC

Linux cloud sessions could not build the runtime or most tests: clang
and GCC -Werror tripped on dead code, false-positive uninitialized
reads, always-false 64-bit overflow checks, and unchecked snprintf
truncation. With warnings tolerated all 18 tests already passed, so the
code was sound; this makes it build cleanly under -Werror on both.

Two of the truncation warnings were real bugs:

- nids.c stored names in 64-byte buffers, but vita-headers db/360 has
  22 mangled C++ names longer than that (up to 96 bytes). They were
  silently cut, so the emitted HLE symbol named a function nothing
  implements. Buffers are now 128 bytes and an over-long name is left
  unresolved instead of truncated; the emitter also falls back to the
  vita_hle_nid_ spelling when a name does not fit its symbol buffer.
- hle_fios.c path_join truncated overlay paths, which can name a
  different file. It now reports truncation and the lookup fails.

Other changes: -Wno-missing-field-initializers on GCC/clang, matching
MSVC, because VITA_GPU_INIT deliberately initializes only the ABI
size/version header; the unused kernel-arena allocator is marked
maybe-unused; dead GPU validation helpers are removed.

New test: nids (fails on the old loader at the 96-byte name).
Verified: clang and GCC Release/Debug, zero warnings, 19/19 CTest.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019w9qd9hR6npnFTCKgz4eBT
